@startuml Digi Bank - Jakarta EE to Spring Boot Migration

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

title Digi Bank\nJakarta EE to Spring Boot Migration

node "Jakarta EE implementation\n(legacy reference)" as jee {
    artifact "Jakarta REST / CDI" as jaxrs
    artifact "JPA / EntityManager" as jeeJpa
    artifact "WildFly runtime" as wildflyOld
    artifact "Java 17 baseline" as java17
}

node "Migration drivers" as decision {
    artifact "Preserve domain scope\nand module boundaries" as preserve
    artifact "Reduce configuration\nand environment dependency" as simplify
    artifact "Improve feedback\nand test automation" as testability
    artifact "Enable application-owned runtime\nwhile retaining WAR/WildFly" as compatibility
}

node "Spring Boot implementation\n(current main)" as sb {
    artifact "Spring Web / MVC" as web
    artifact "Spring Data JPA" as springJpa
    artifact "Embedded Tomcat\nfor development" as tomcat
    artifact "SpringBootServletInitializer\nfor WAR deployment" as initializer
    artifact "Java 21 baseline" as java21
}

jee --> decision: baseline and lessons
decision --> sb: controlled re-platforming

jaxrs --> web: REST contract retained
jeeJpa --> springJpa: persistence model retained
wildflyOld --> initializer: production option retained
java17 --> java21: supported baseline uplift

note right of decision
  The decision is operational, not ideological:
  reduce the distance between source code,
  local runtime, CI validation, and deployment.
end note

note bottom of sb
  Delivered outcome: same modular-monolith shape,
  more accessible runtime and test workflow.
end note

@enduml
